Abstract = {Edge computing supports a wide range of real-time use cases across
   diverse domains. However, the rapid emergence of Artificial Intelligence
   (AI) use cases such as smart aging and intelligent video surveillance is
   introducing complex requirements that existing edge architectures are
   not designed to handle. Addressing these requirements requires a
   comprehensive rethink of how edge infrastructure is delivered. This
   article highlights emerging AI use cases and outlines the architectural
   and operational requirements and challenges that must be addressed to
   enable the effective deployment of next-generation AI at the edge.},
