Month = {NOV 15},
Abstract = {Integrated sensing and communication (ISAC) has emerged as a key
   component of modern communication technologies that are driven by rapid
   advancements in wireless sensor networks (WSNs). The increasing adoption
   of the Internet of Things (IoT) and the Industrial Internet of Things
   (IIoT) is transforming various walks of life by enabling a diverse range
   of functional applications. As automation and connectivity continue to
   evolve, ISAC plays a crucial role in ensuring seamless communication and
   real-time data sensing, establishing itself as a fundamental pillar of
   contemporary technological ecosystems. Notably, ISAC offers several
   advantages over systems that rely on separate transceivers and
   receivers, including reduced costs, enhanced spectral efficiency, and
   improved energy efficiency. This review article provides a comprehensive
   overview of the core radar topologies employed in ISAC communication
   systems and examines the corresponding localization algorithms that
   align with these specific radar configurations. Furthermore, the study
   analyzes key parameters that can directly influence the performance of
   the localization estimation process within ISAC systems. Once a
   communication system is deployed, an important consideration is its
   energy consumption. To address this, the review highlights the
   relationship between energy usage and the types of antennas employed.
   Furthermore, we examine the emerging trends and techniques in ISAC
   systems, focusing on their role in optimizing and enhancing various
   communication applications such as channel estimation. We conclude this
   article by outlining limitations and some open challenges for future
   research directions in the localization of nodes in ISAC systems,
   providing insights into potential advancements.},
