Month = {MAR 1},
Abstract = {This study introduces a novel deep learning-based system for the
   automatic segmentation and detection of wheat stem rust. The study
   utilized wheat crop images from a standard data resource. Using this
   collected images, the Vision Transformer-based MobileUnet++
   (ViT-MUnet++) segments the crop image and allows for better detection.
   Subsequently, the ``segmented images{''} are processed by the Adaptive
   Recurrent Mobilenetv2 with Long Short-Term Memory Layer (ARMV2-LSTM),
   and parameters are tuned using Enhanced Random Functionbased Sparrow
   Search Algorithm (ERF-SSA). Further, the implemented ERF-SSA-ARMV2-LSTM
   was compared with several models and achieved an accuracy of 91.61 \%,
   which is enhanced than the conventional approaches like CNN, CycleGAN,
   DNN, and ARMV2-LSTM. This showed that the proposed technique can
   effectively detect and grade the WSR at an early stage.},
